# Lorenz 84: a low-order model of the general circulation of the atmosphere (E. N. Lorenz, Tellus A 36, 98-110, 1984)
# x is the strength of the westerly wind, y and z the cosine and sine phases of a chain of travelling eddies.
# F and G are the thermal forcings; a=0.25, b=4, F=8, G=1 give a chaotic attractor. Lower F (try F=6) for periodic flow,
# and continue in F to see the Hopf bifurcation of the steady westerly flow.
x'=-y^2-z^2-a*x+a*f
y'=x*y-b*x*z-y+g
z'=b*x*y+x*z-z
par a=0.25,b=4,f=8,g=1
init x=1,y=0,z=0
#@range f 0 10
#@range g 0 2
@ total=200,dt=0.02,trans=20,xp=y,yp=z,zp=x
@ xlo=-2.5,xhi=3,ylo=-2.5,yhi=2.5
done
